{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_012hpqrChPBQHsNgaoCgsSz4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Here's what was written for **Q9: Instruction tuning vs pre-training**:\n\n---\n\n**Core distinction:**\n- **Pre-training** = *what to know* — CLM loss on all tokens across trillions of raw text tokens. Teaches world knowledge, language patterns. One-time, massively expensive (Llama 3 8B: 15T tokens, weeks on thousands of H100s).\n- **Instruction tuning (SFT)** = *how to behave* — CE loss applied **only on response tokens** (instruction tokens are masked). Teaches instruction-following, format, style. Cheap and repeatable with LoRA (hours on 4× A100s).\n\n**Key production insight called out:** Instruction tuning does **not** reliably inject new facts — it shapes format/behavior, so if the base model never saw your domain data, IT will produce confident hallucinations. For knowledge gaps, use RAG or domain-adaptive pre-training (DAPT: CLM on raw domain text like PubMed or legal filings).\n\n**Three pitfalls covered:**\n1. Saying IT teaches new information (it doesn't — RAG or DAPT for facts)\n2. Thinking product teams pre-train from scratch (they don't — they start from Llama 3/Mistral/Qwen)\n3. Not knowing the loss function difference (CLM on all tokens vs CE on response tokens only)"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":343,"cache_read_input_tokens":68315,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":343,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0e2b2fce-89a9-41c8-9844-ffa6aeb7deb7","uuid":"6729fdf2-16a6-44cd-a83e-132d3976ea75"}
